WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.012
Coding Exercise 5 asks you to rank salaries within
each department while

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:08.638
keeping each employee row Because the detail rows
must remain use a

00:00:08.662 --> 00:00:13.175
window function rather than collapsing the data with
GROUP BY The required

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.550
expression is RANK followed by OVER Inside OVER
PARTITION BY department creates

00:00:18.562 --> 00:00:23.900
a separate ranking population for each department
ORDER BY salary descending makes

00:00:23.912 --> 00:00:28.188
the highest salary rank one Give the result a clear
alias such

00:00:28.212 --> 00:00:34.412
as department_rank The final ORDER BY controls the
display of rows It

00:00:34.438 --> 00:00:37.925
can order by department and salary descending so the
result is easy

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:43.550
to inspect Run and Check When the department changes
verify that

00:00:43.575 --> 00:00:49.300
the ranking starts again Also notice what happens if
salaries tie RANK

00:00:49.312 --> 00:00:52.262
assigns the same rank to equal values and may skip
the next

00:00:52.288 --> 00:00:58.038
numeric rank This exercise reinforces a key
window-function idea PARTITION BY groups

00:00:58.062 --> 00:01:01.588
rows for the calculation but it does not remove the
individual rows

00:01:01.612 --> 00:01:02.362
from the result
